#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:5
msgid "LeapRAID Driver for Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:8
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:10
msgid ""
"LeapRAID is a storage RAID controller driver developed by LeapIO Tech Inc. "
"The controller targets enterprise storage, cloud infrastructure, high "
"performance computing (HPC), and AI workloads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:14
msgid ""
"It provides high-performance storage virtualization over PCI Express Gen4 "
"and supports both SAS and SATA HDDs and SSDs. It offers both Host Bus "
"Adapter and RAID modes to meet diverse deployment requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:19
msgid "Supported devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:21
msgid "LeapHBA-8200C"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:24
msgid "Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:26
msgid "PCIe Gen4 x8 host interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:27
msgid "Support for SAS and SATA devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:28
msgid "RAID levels: 0, 1, 10, 5, 50, 6, 60"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:29
msgid "Advanced error handling and end-to-end data integrity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:32
msgid "LeapRAID specific host attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:40
msgid ""
"The host \"fw_queue_depth\" read-only attribute shows the firmware queue "
"depth of the host."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:43
msgid ""
"The host \"host_sas_address\" read-only attribute shows the SAS address of "
"the host."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:46
msgid ""
"The host \"board_name\" read-only attribute shows the board name reported by "
"manufacturing page 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:50
msgid "LeapRAID specific disk attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:58
msgid ""
"The read-only attribute \"sas_device_handle\" represents the disk's device "
"handle, which is a unique identifier maintained by the firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:61
msgid ""
"The read-only attribute \"sas_ncq_prio_supported\" reports whether a SATA "
"device supports NCQ command priority."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:64
msgid ""
"The attribute \"sas_ncq_prio_enable\" controls NCQ command priority. A value "
"of 0 disables NCQ priority handling for RT-priority I/O. Writing 1 enables "
"NCQ priority handling when the device reports support for the feature "
"through VPD page 0x89. Writes to unsupported devices fail with an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:70
msgid "LeapRAID module parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:72
msgid ""
"The following module parameters can be configured at driver load time to "
"control driver behavior and tuning options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:76
msgid "1. open_pcie_trace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:78
msgid ""
"This parameter controls whether PCIe transaction tracing is enabled in the "
"driver. When set to 1, PCIe trace collection is enabled by default, allowing "
"detailed tracing of PCIe operations for debugging and performance analysis. "
"Setting it to 0 disables the trace functionality to reduce overhead in "
"production environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:85
msgid "2. enable_mp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:87
msgid ""
"This parameter enables or disables multipath support for target devices. "
"When set to 1, multipath functionality is enabled (default), allowing "
"multiple paths to be established. Setting it to 0 disables multipath "
"handling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:93
msgid "3. max_msix_vectors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:95
msgid ""
"This parameter sets the upper limit on the number of MSI-X interrupt vectors "
"that the driver will request during initialization. The default value of -1 "
"allows the driver to use all available vectors as provided by the device. "
"Setting a positive integer restricts the number of vectors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:101
msgid "4. poll_queues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scsi/leapraid.rst:103
msgid ""
"This parameter specifies the number of I/O queues to be used when operating "
"in io_uring poll mode. The default value is 0."
msgstr ""

